In the News
Executive View
Del-desiran=E2=80=99s Phase 3 failure materially weakens both Novartis=E2=80=
=99s $12 billion Avidity acquisition thesis and confidence in extrapolating m=
uscle RNA knockdown into functional benefit.
The miss does not invalidate antibody-oligonucleotide conjugates, but undiscl=
osed secondary results provide no credible basis yet for regulatory salvage.
Amgen=E2=80=99s Imdelltra crossed into first-line small-cell lung cancer.
The DLL3 T-cell engager improved overall survival as maintenance after chemo-=
immunotherapy, potentially extending treatment to patients who would never re=
ach second line; undisclosed effect sizes remain the critical limitation.
FDA established muscle-directed therapy as a new layer of spinal muscular atr=
ophy treatment.
Isembyld=E2=80=99s approval creates an add-on market for residual weakness de=
spite SMN2-targeted therapy, although the benefit is moderate, treatment requ=
ires monthly infusions and fractures warrant monitoring.
Convenience is becoming a credible source of clinical differentiation in here=
ditary angioedema.
Once-daily deucrictibant produced an 83% placebo-adjusted reduction in attack=
s, potentially allowing Pharvaris to offer oral on-demand and preventive form=
ulations within one franchise.
Pediatric obesity treatment moved materially earlier.
Semaglutide moved 40% of treated children aged 6=E2=80=9311 below the obesity=
 threshold, but Novo Nordisk has not yet disclosed the primary mean BMI effec=
t, discontinuation data or full safety results.
Strategy Narrative
Del-desiran turns Novartis=E2=80=99s Avidity bet into an endpoint and platfor=
m-reproducibility problem
What changed
On September 8, Novartis reported that the approximately 150-patient Phase 3 =
HARBOR trial in myotonic dystrophy type 1 failed to improve video hand-openin=
g time versus placebo after 54 weeks. The company reported unspecified =E2=80=
=9Cclinical activity=E2=80=9D on secondary and exploratory measures but discl=
osed no effect sizes. Safety was generally consistent with prior studies. (
Novartis
;
SEC filing
) (
novartis.com
)
What it tells us
This extends last Monday=E2=80=99s emphasis on functional evidence over targe=
t engagement. Earlier del-desiran studies demonstrated delivery into muscle a=
nd DMPK-mRNA reduction, but HARBOR did not convert that biology into success =
on its prespecified pivotal endpoint. Because video hand-opening time is a no=
vel measure focused on myotonia rather than overall disability, endpoint sele=
ction may have contributed; however, absent quantitative results for grip str=
ength, DM1-Activ, muscle testing and mobility, the program should be valued a=
s failed rather than merely delayed.
The commercial impact is broader than one rare-disease asset. Del-desiran was=
 the most advanced validation opportunity within Novartis=E2=80=99s $12 billi=
on acquisition of Avidity. The failure therefore reduces the acquisition=E2=
=80=99s risk-adjusted value and raises the evidentiary bar for sister program=
s del-zota in Duchenne muscular dystrophy and del-brax in facioscapulohumeral=
 muscular dystrophy. It does not establish a class failure because those prog=
rams use different oligonucleotide payloads and address different biology. (
fiercebiotech.com
)
What to watch next
The complete secondary-endpoint dataset; whether FDA entertains an alternativ=
e development path; and whether Novartis changes the regulatory or commercial=
 assumptions for del-zota and del-brax.
Imdelltra could move T-cell engagement into routine first-line SCLC maintenan=
ce
What changed
Amgen=E2=80=99s 563-patient Phase 3 DeLLphi-305 trial met its overall-surviva=
l endpoint at a prespecified interim analysis. Imdelltra plus durvalumab also=
 improved progression-free survival and response rate versus durvalumab alone=
 in patients whose extensive-stage small-cell lung cancer had not progressed =
after durvalumab, platinum chemotherapy and etoposide. No efficacy magnitudes=
 were disclosed. The company reported no unexpected safety signal, with short=
 monitoring periods required after the first two Imdelltra infusions. (
Amgen
) (
amgen.com
)
What it tells us
Imdelltra previously demonstrated a major survival benefit after progression;=
 DeLLphi-305 now suggests DLL3-directed T-cell engagement can improve outcome=
s before relapse. That is strategically important in SCLC because many patien=
ts deteriorate too quickly to receive later-line therapy.
The trial also supports a sequencing model in which intensive chemo-immunothe=
rapy induction is followed by immune maintenance escalation rather than addit=
ional cytotoxic therapy. Commercial value will depend on whether the survival=
 gain justifies chronic infusion, early cytokine-release and neurologic-risk =
management, and the added cost of combining two branded immunotherapies.
What to watch next
Median survival, hazard ratios, treatment discontinuations, grade 3/4 infecti=
ons and cytokine-release syndrome=E2=80=94and whether benefit extends across =
patients with brain metastases.
Isembyld establishes combination treatment for residual SMA disability
What changed
FDA approved Scholar Rock=E2=80=99s Isembyld, or apitegromab, for adults and =
children aged two and older receiving an SMN2-targeted treatment. In the cont=
rolled SAPPHIRE trial, monthly 10 mg/kg infusions produced a 2.2-point placeb=
o-adjusted improvement on the Hammersmith motor scale; 34.2% achieved a clini=
cally meaningful three-point improvement versus 13.5% with placebo. The stron=
gest controlled evidence came from nonambulatory children aged 2=E2=80=9312. =
FDA highlighted an increased fracture risk. (
FDA
;
Scholar Rock
) (
fda.gov
)
What it tells us
SMA is shifting from replacement of missing SMN protein toward multidimension=
al combination care. Isembyld does not compete directly with Spinraza, Evrysd=
i or gene replacement; it addresses persistent muscle weakness after motor-ne=
uron rescue.
The mean benefit is meaningful but not transformative, and monthly intravenou=
s administration adds substantial burden. Commercial adoption is therefore li=
kely to concentrate initially among patients who remain functionally impaired=
 despite stable SMN-directed treatment. Payers may demand documented plateau =
or decline before authorizing an indefinite add-on biologic.
What to watch next
Adult uptake, ambulatory evidence, durability beyond one year, fracture incid=
ence and whether muscle-directed treatment expands to other neuromuscular dis=
eases.
Oral prophylaxis and earlier obesity treatment expand chronic-therapy frontie=
rs
Pharvaris=E2=80=99s 85-patient Phase 3 CHAPTER-3 trial showed an 83% reductio=
n in hereditary-angioedema attacks versus placebo with once-daily deucrictiba=
nt XR; the reduction was 87% among type 1 and type 2 patients. No treatment-r=
elated serious adverse events were reported. The result is compelling but bas=
ed on a small, 24-week trial, and absolute attack rates have not been disclos=
ed=E2=80=94making cross-trial comparisons with injectable prophylactics prema=
ture. If confirmed, the immediate- and extended-release formulations could gi=
ve Pharvaris a differentiated oral franchise spanning rescue and prevention. (
Pharvaris
) (
ir.pharvaris.com
)
Separately, Novo Nordisk reported that 40.4% of children aged 6=E2=80=9311 re=
ceiving semaglutide plus lifestyle intervention were no longer classified as =
having obesity after 68 weeks, versus none on placebo. More than 85% had seve=
re obesity at baseline, and no growth or pubertal-development signal was iden=
tified. The finding strengthens medical treatment of severe pediatric obesity=
, but the withheld mean BMI result, treatment-estimand framing and need for l=
ong-term therapy limit interpretation until presentation at ObesityWeek in No=
vember. (
Novo Nordisk
) (
novonordisk.com
)
Additional Company and Regulatory Signals
Biohaven=E2=80=99s epilepsy licensing thesis acquired a toxicology overhang.
FDA paused new enrollment in BHV-7000 trials because available data were insu=
fficient to assess the human risk of a metabolite found during rodent testing=
. More than 600 randomized patients may continue dosing, and one pivotal foca=
l-epilepsy trial is fully enrolled, preserving the planned second-half readou=
t. SK Biopharmaceuticals had received the underlying data before signing its =
licensing agreement, reducing transaction-surprise risk but not eventual appr=
oval risk. (
SEC filing
) (
sec.gov
)
HER2-mutant lung cancer gained a second first-line targeted option.
FDA expanded Bayer=E2=80=99s Hyrnuo to untreated advanced disease after a sin=
gle-arm study produced a 75% response rate; 38% of responders remained in res=
ponse for at least 12 months. The accelerated approval creates direct competi=
tion with already-approved zongertinib, but comparative durability and toxici=
ty=E2=80=94not response rate alone=E2=80=94will determine sequencing. (
FDA
) (
fda.gov
)
FDA codified a lower-friction pathway for cardiovascular AI alerts.
A final order effective September 11 classified machine-learning notification=
 software as Class II, allowing future substantially equivalent products to u=
se the 510(k) pathway. Special controls explicitly address clinical performan=
ce, model bias and generalizability, human factors and overreliance. The like=
ly strategic effect is faster category expansion=E2=80=94and greater commodit=
ization of stand-alone alerts=E2=80=94shifting differentiation toward proprie=
tary data, workflow integration and demonstrated impact on downstream care. (
Federal Register
) (
govinfo.gov
)
What I=E2=80=99m Watching Next
Quantitative HARBOR secondary endpoints and implications for the remaining Av=
idity-derived programs.
Full DeLLphi-305 survival and safety data.
Real-world payer criteria and adoption for Isembyld combination therapy.
Absolute attack rates and longer-term safety for deucrictibant.
Detailed STEP Young BMI, discontinuation and post-treatment data.
The fully enrolled BHV-7000 pivotal readout despite the partial clinical hold.
Bottom Line
This week again separated biological activity from clinically and commerciall=
y usable benefit. Del-desiran reduced disease-associated RNA in earlier studi=
es but failed its pivotal functional test. Imdelltra, by contrast, extended a=
 proven mechanism into an earlier and larger treatment setting, while Isembyl=
d converted a moderate motor benefit into an entirely new combination layer f=
or SMA.
The strategic premium is increasingly accruing to therapies that do more than=
 engage biology: they must choose defensible endpoints, fit into existing tre=
atment sequences and offer sufficient efficacy or convenience to justify chro=
nic cost and operational burden.
Informational only; not investment advice.

